_callback_outcome` covers a third party being sent back to the holder, and the documents give no close code for that either. This is also marked as unresolved.\n\nThe rest of the file is unchanged, apart from the source text for the callbacks and updated wording in the `unresolved` entries.\n\n**Decision for you:** if the bank would rather close these third-party and deceased cases with `VOID` and no reason, both outcomes are easy to change. I didn't do that because the codes sheet allows leaving the reason out only where it lists \"none,\" and `VOID` doesn't."}
{"event": "policy_compiled", "run_id": "2515783044444e5381b3551ac198ece3", "pid": 131879, "time": "2026-10-10T23:54:04-0700", "elapsed_s": 232.582, "artifact": "out/ext-kurilian.policy.json", "bands": 1, "identity_fields": ["sec_code"], "special_cases": ["dispute", "refuse_to_talk", "human", "restructuring", "scam"], "unresolved": [{"topic": "bands / deadline", "text": "There is no k-date and no upper limit. A promise date is recordable when today or any business day after today. The schema requires a band with a deadline, so one band covers dl_days 1-90 (openapi.json range) and its deadline is a placeholder of 36500 calendar days that stands for 'no upper limit'; the documents give no deadline value.", "doc": "sources/000-01-call-sheet.md"}, {"topic": "persuasion attempts", "text": "Zero persuasion attempts in any band. The first \"no\" from the customer ends the call: close `No-PTP` / `R07`.", "doc": "sources/000-01-call-sheet.md"}, {"topic": "below-full proposal sentence", "text": "A proposal below the full amount: EXACTLY \"That is below what we can take.\" Then close `No-PTP` / `R07`. No phrase field holds this sentence.", "doc": "sources/000-01-call-sheet.md"}, {"topic": "vague date", "text": "A vague period (\"later\", \"after payday\", \"soon\"): ask once for the exact day. If still vague, close `No-PTP` / `R07` (no deadline fallback).", "doc": "sources/000-01-call-sheet.md"}, {"topic": "third-party sentence and outcome", "text": "Third party: Say EXACTLY: \"Please ask {{title}} {{last_name}} to call us on the number printed on their statement.\" No callback; the documents give no close outcome for a non-wrong-number third party. The schema requires one, so the holder-not-confirmed code VOID / JCB-unclear is used for no_callback_outcome and (unused, callback disabled) scheduled_outcome.", "doc": "sources/000-01-call-sheet.md"}, {"topic": "deceased", "text": "The documents do not address a deceased account holder; no deceased sentence. The schema requires an outcome, so the holder-not-confirmed code VOID / JCB-unclear is used as the closest listed code.", "doc": "sources/001-02-codes.txt"}, {"topic": "already_paid", "text": "No \"already paid\" rule. The customer never gets the one-business-day sentence and no paid note. \"it was paid off and closed\" is handled with the dispute case (close `No-PTP` / `R07`).", "doc": "sources/000-01-call-sheet.md"}, {"topic": "hardship", "text": "No hardship rule. The customer never gets sympathy for illness, bereavement or job loss.", "doc": "sources/000-01-call-sheet.md"}, {"topic": "today question", "text": "The documents do not dictate a question about paying today; after the debt intro they say only: Then state amt_due and dl_days.", "doc": "sources/000-01-call-sheet.md"}, {"topic": "write failure sentence", "text": "A second failure \u2192 close `No-PTP` / `R07` and say the write failed.", "doc": "sources/000-01-call-sheet.md"}, {"topic": "promise then transfer", "text": "The documents do not say which outcome applies when a promise was recorded and the call is then transferred; default kept.", "doc": "sources/000-01-call-sheet.md"}], "audit_fixed": ["third_party.callback.source: cited the supervisor mail together with the call sheet's own 'DO NOT book a callback' rule, because the two documents agree.", "notes.source: changed to the supervisor mail ('no notes') and listed the call sheet and codes file as agreeing. Nothing about how notes work was changed.", "Checked every other value against the documents and the API enums (sec_code, prod_kind loan, kcb_desk, PTP/No-PTP/DEC/VOID/transferred, R07/F01/F02/RNG/JCB-unclear/kcb_person). All are supported; no other changes were needed. The three documents do not conflict."], "audit_unresolved": ["The documents define no days-late bands and no deadline, so bands is empty. The validator needs at least one band, and making one up would invent a threshold.", "No question about paying today is dictated, so today_question is empty.", "The third-party sentence and the below-full-proposal sentence have no phrase field. The documents give no close outcome for a third party who is not a wrong number.", "The documents do not say what to say when the write fails; they only say to say that it failed.", "Deceased account holder is not covered.", "Promise recorded and then a transfer: the documents do not say which outcome wins; the default is kept.", "Hardship and already-paid have no rule; statements of that kind have no defined route other than the dispute wording ('it was paid off and closed').", "The callback and deceased outcome pairs stay empty because callbacks are not used and deceased is not covered. A strict check of these pairs may flag them as empty."], "defaulted_without_source": [], "unknown_special_cases": [], "api_mapping_notes": []}
